+  "description": "The console's URL scheme. The hash names the tab (app.js showView) and the query string carries the scope, so a permalink, a reload and a tab switch are one operation. Values are encodeURIComponent-encoded and decoded with URLSearchParams; keys are plain. write() merges into the live query: an empty value removes its key, unknown keys are preserved in place, existing keys keep their order and new keys append. A value write() would refuse is never put in the URL, so anything read() rejects could only have been typed by hand. Tab switches stay on history.replaceState (Paul's ruling C); pushState is never used. Orientation only - the examples are the contract. v2 (S6, 2026-09-17): up to four PAC evidence panes, each addressed by a PREFIXED key (a.source, a.id, a.committee, a.cycle ... d.*) so `cycle` goes on belonging to Graph and \"whose cycle is this?\" stays answerable. The pane's search text is transient and is never written; `category` carries the committee-type filter in the same spelling Graph uses. A fifth prefix is not a key this module knows, so e.id is preserved in the query and never read as scope.",
